{"pageid": 1419, "title": "Something Is Killing the Children (film)", "revid": 2981, "categories": ["Production"], "html": "<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p class=\"mw-empty-elt\">\n</p><aside role=\"region\" class=\"portable-infobox pi-background pi-border-color pi-theme-wikia pi-layout-default\">\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-item-spacing pi-title pi-secondary-background\" data-source=\"title1\">Something Is Killing the Children</h2>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n\t<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">Information</h2>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"director\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Director</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><span class=\"new\" title=\"Craig Zobel (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvQ3JhaWdfWm9iZWw/YWN0aW9uPWVkaXQmcmVkbGluaz0x\">Craig Zobel</span></div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"distributor\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Distributor</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Blumhouse\" title=\"Blumhouse\">Blumhouse</a></div>\n</div>\n\n</section>\n</aside>\n\n<p class=\"mw-empty-elt\"></p><p><i><b>Something Is Killing the Children</b></i> is an upcoming live-action supernatural horror film produced by <a href=\"/wiki/Blumhouse\" title=\"Blumhouse\">Blumhouse</a> based on the <a href=\"/wiki/Something_Is_Killing_the_Children_(comic_series)\" title=\"Something Is Killing the Children (comic series)\">comic series</a> of the same name from co-creators <a href=\"/wiki/James_Tynion_IV\" title=\"James Tynion IV\">James Tynion IV</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/Werther_Dell%27Edera\" title=\"Werther Dell&#39;Edera\">Werther Dell'Edera</a>. The film will be produced by Tynion and Stephen Christy, and directed by <span class=\"new\" title=\"Craig Zobel (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvQ3JhaWdfWm9iZWw/YWN0aW9uPWVkaXQmcmVkbGluaz0x\">Craig Zobel</span>.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup><sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-2\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Synopsis\">Synopsis</span></h2>\n<p>TBA\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Credits\">Credits</span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Main_cast\">Main cast</span></h3>\n<p>TBA\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Crew\">Crew</span></h3>\n<ul><li><span class=\"new\" title=\"Craig Zobel (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvQ3JhaWdfWm9iZWw/YWN0aW9uPWVkaXQmcmVkbGluaz0x\">Craig Zobel</span> <small>(director)</small></li>\n<li>Stephen Christy <small>(producer)</small></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/James_Tynion_IV\" title=\"James Tynion IV\">James Tynion IV</a> <small>(producer)</small></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Werther_Dell%27Edera\" title=\"Werther Dell&#39;Edera\">Werther Dell'Edera</a> <small>(co-producer)</small></li>\n<li>Adam Yoelin <small>(executive producer)</small></li>\n<li>Mette Norkjaer <small>(executive producer)</small></li>\n<li>Shaun Sutton <small>(executive producer)</small></li>\n<li>Ryan Turek <small>(executive producer)</small></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Production\">Production</span></h2>\n<p>On July 23, 2026, during a signing and Q&amp;A on Trinity Comics’ Whatnot stream, <a href=\"/wiki/James_Tynion_IV\" title=\"James Tynion IV\">James Tynion IV</a> revealed that there is a completed screenplay for the live-action film, but the delay is due to the companion <a href=\"/wiki/Something_Is_Killing_the_Children_(TV_series)\" title=\"Something Is Killing the Children (TV series)\">animated series</a>. The creative team wants to complete the \"series bible\" for the animated series before taking both adaptations out to studios and streamers simultaneously in hopes of finding a partner interested in both projects, though Tynion noted that if a buyer only wants the live-action film, the animated series can still be shopped elsewhere.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-3\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"References\">References</span></h2>\n<div class=\"mw-references-wrap\"><ol class=\"references\">\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-1\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-1\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer noopener\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-news/something-is-killing-the-children-movie-blumhouse-1236409897/\">Horror Comic ‘Something Is Killing the Children’ Getting Movie and Series Adaptations in Blumhouse Deal (Exclusive) - The Hollywood Reporter</a></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-2\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-2\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer noopener\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://deadline.com/2026/10/something-is-killing-the-children-movie-craig-zobel-blumhouse-1237153820/\">Craig Zobel &amp; Blumhouse Teaming On ‘Something Is Killing The Children’ - Deadline</a></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-3\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-3\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer noopener\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.dreadcentral.com/comics-books/582354/james-tynion-iv-reveals-major-update-on-blumhouses-something-is-killing-the-children-movie-and-animated-series/\">James Tynion IV Reveals Major Update on Blumhouse’s ‘Something Is Killing the Children’ Movie and Animated Series - Dread Central</a></span>\n</li>\n</ol></div></div>", "fetched_at": "2026-10-28T22:43:43+00:00"}